  "id": "adequate-sample",
  "term": "adequate sample",
  "definition": "In research methods, an adequate sample is a group of participants that is large and appropriate enough to answer the study’s question credibly. In qualitative work, this is commonly judged by whether additional interviews are no longer adding important new information or meaning.",
